     "description": "Reference: fire_behavior's Interp_profile (the routine WRF's Interp_wrfwinds_to_cfbm and the standalone Calc_fire_wind both call) replayed by the EarthSciML feedback driver (data/eqwefic/fire_build/feedback_driver) on the nearest WRF column of test7/wrf.nc frame 10 (t = 10 s) for fire cell (1,1), linking the instrumented firelib (real32, commit 8d519c6). A Fortran-generated regime: the fire wind height is overridden to exercise a branch that test7 (1 m) never reaches. Single precision: rel 1e-5. Regime: fire_wind_height = 6.096 m (WRF default): still the first-layer branch (hgt_1 ~ 16 m). The WRF path passes kfde = 45 w-levels (kdmax = 43) where this component's NZW = 44 gives kdmax = 42; the branch selected here is far below either bound.",
