    {
     "id": "standalone_call10_cell_9_14",
     "description": "The atmosphere column that feeds the FIRE FRONT, added 2026-09-21. Every other standalone regime of this component comes from the 10 x 10 block at the domain origin, which is the only part of the tile the fire_wind dump used to cover and which carries no fire in test7; column (9, 14) is the one nearest fire cell (18, 64), the cell couplings/wildlandfire_behavior.esm is built on. Reached by widening the dump from that block to the whole tile (fork ctessum-claude/fire_behavior, io/coupling_mod.F90 Calc_fire_wind); the widened dump reproduces standalone_call10_cell_1_1's expectations exactly, so this is the same run, the same call 10 = step 20, and the same real32 build. rel 1e-5. NOTE this does NOT let the component be mounted in wildlandfire_behavior.esm: Calc_fire_wind runs on the 19 x 19 ATMOSPHERE grid and the fire mesh values are produced afterwards by Interp_horizontal, which is a genuine bilinear interpolation (5593 distinct uf values over the 80 x 80 fire mesh against 361 atmosphere columns) and is not transcribed. The fire cell's wind is therefore not any single column's -- the nearest, this one, differs by 2.2e-3 m/s.",
